      "POL-NS-07: direct the human reviewer to refund the rider's cancellation fee of SGD 4.50 in full (anti-farming escalation packet instruction)."
    ],
    "confidence": 0.9,
    "explanation": "To both parties. The trip-level facts favour the driver, but the platform's anti-farming guard stops this case from closing automatically, so no money moves today.\n\nWhat the record shows. The trip record and the GPS trace agree that the driver reached the pick-up at Blk 12 Telok Blangah Cres at 22:31:15 on 15 Sep and then held position inside the 50 m STANDARD-zone arrival radius for a continuous 408 seconds, on 42 qualifying fixes (POL-NS-01 limbs (a) and (c); 408 s against the 180 s free waiting period in force for this trip). He cancelled at 22:38:07 under reason code RIDER_NO_SHOW, one of the three codes POL-NS-01 limb (d) recognises, with no boarding event — 6 minutes 50 seconds of waiting. The arrival marker was not false under POL-NS-05: at the moment he tapped 'I'm Here' the trace puts him 0.11 m from the pin and stationary (0.0 km/h), so the waiting clock is not reset. POL-NS-06 does not apply — the dwell was not short — and the MISSING traffic advisory EV-ADVIS-02751-01 (weight 0.0) changes nothing, because there is only one in-geofence interval to measure. The fare ledger's SGD 4.50 cancellation fee matches the SGD 4.50 in force for this trip, so there is no POL-NS-08(d) defect.\n\nThe rider is not exonerated by POL-NS-04. The only chat message in the window is the driver's ('im at the pickup point', sent 22:31:35, read 22:32:05); the rider sent no locating or coordinating message, so limb (a) fails and the clause cannot help her. Her own device track sits 851–858 m from the pin (mean 854.6 m), with none of her 70 fixes inside the 100 m presence radius — consistent with her not being at the pick-up point. Her profile does not decide anything either way: no_show_disputes_30d is 0 and disputes_with_counterparty_90d is 0, and prior_no_show_flags is context only under POL-GEN-01.\n\nWhy the case escalates. Normally the SGD 4.50 fee would stand and POL-NS-07 would pay the driver 80% of it, SGD 3.60. But the POL-NS-07 anti-farming check trips on the driver's own profile: 4 no-show terminations in the last 30 days (the clause threshold is 4 or more) and 4 ÷ 40 completed trips = 0.10, above the 0.08 rate limb. Both advocates conceded this point on the arithmetic. Compensation is therefore withheld and the case goes to human review under POL-NS-09(d).\n\nWhat this means. The ruling is ESCALATE, which is terminal: no refund issues to the rider and no payment issues to the driver, and the disputed SGD 4.50 is held rather than collected or refunded while a person reviews the file. The escalation packet carries the POL-NS-07 instruction that the reviewer is to refund the SGD 4.50 in full if the pattern is confirmed. The open question the reviewer must settle is whether the driver's 4 no-show terminations in 30 days reflect genuine no-shows like this one or fee-farming; the trip-level evidence here shows a properly performed pick-up.\n\nConfidence is 0.9. The deciding facts rest on the GPS trace (EV-GPS-02751), the trip record (EV-TRIP-02751) and the driver profile (EV-DPROF-02751), each at full weight 1.0, so the POL-GEN-02(2) cap is 1.0; the missing advisory at weight 0.0 is not relied on. One claim from each side resting on that missing advisory was discarded at the mechanical stage for citing the impaired artifact without naming its issue code, as POL-GEN-02(1) requires. This ruling was made without human review and is provisional; either party may appeal it once within 30 days under POL-GEN-04."
  },
