{
  "ruling": {
    "ruling": "ESCALATE",
    "amount_sgd": null,
    "driver_compensation_sgd": null,
    "referrals": [
      "POL-NS-07: the escalation packet must direct the human reviewer to refund the rider's cancellation fee of SGD 4.50 in full. The disputed SGD 4.50 is held by the automated pipeline meanwhile — not collected and not refunded — pending review."
    ],
    "confidence": 0.9,
    "explanation": "The record here is unusually clean, and the two sides actually agree about it; the outcome turns on the driver's own profile.\n\nWHAT HAPPENED. The trip record (EV-TRIP-02751, weight 1.0) shows the driver assigned at 22:22:34, tapped 'I'm Here' at 22:31:15, the free waiting timer started at 22:31:17, and the driver cancelled at 22:38:07 with reason code RIDER_NO_SHOW. The driver's GPS trace (EV-GPS-02751, weight 1.0) places him inside the STANDARD-zone rendezvous radius of 50 m for one continuous qualifying run of 408 seconds, 22:31:15 to 22:38:03, with 42 qualifying fixes. The free waiting period in force (EV-TRIP-02751.platform_policy.free_wait_sec) is 180 seconds, so the dwell required by POL-NS-01(c) was met and the cancellation at 22:38:07 fell after that dwell elapsed at 22:34:15. POL-NS-01 limbs (a) to (d) all hold.\n\nNO CLAUSE DISPLACES THE FEE. The arrival marker is not false under POL-NS-05: at the marker the driver was stationary at the pin (minimum distance 0.11 m; speed 0.0 kph), not more than 300 m away and not travelling at 15 kph or more, so the waiting clock is not recomputed. The dwell exceeds the minimum, so POL-NS-06's premature-cancellation route does not open. POL-NS-03 does not apply because the driver was inside the arrival radius, not outside it. POL-NS-04 cannot exonerate the rider: it needs a locating or coordinating message from the rider, and the chat log (EV-CHAT-02751, weight 1.0) holds one message, sent by the driver at 22:31:35 and read at 22:32:05. The rider's device track shows 70 fixes, none inside the 100 m STANDARD rider-presence radius, sitting 851–858 m from the pin throughout — she was not at the pickup point. The fare ledger (EV-FARE-02751, weight 1.0) charges SGD 4.50, which reconciles exactly with platform_policy.cancellation_fee_sgd of SGD 4.50, so there is no POL-NS-08(d) defect.\n\nWHY THIS DOES NOT BECOME A DRIVER PAYOUT. POL-NS-07 would fix the driver's compensation at 80% of SGD 4.50, i.e. SGD 3.60. But the anti-farming guard on the driver's own profile (EV-DPROF-02751, weight 1.0) trips: no_show_terminations_30d is 4 (the absolute limb requires 4 or more) and 4 divided by completed_trips_30d of 40 is 0.10, which is above the 0.08 rate limb. Both limbs are met. Compensation is therefore withheld and the case escalates under POL-NS-09(d). Both advocates conceded this point candidly, and the arithmetic is on the record.\n\nTHE CONSEQUENCE. Escalation under POL-NS-09 is terminal: no money moves now. The disputed SGD 4.50 is held rather than collected or refunded while a human reviewer decides. The escalation trigger is POL-NS-09(d) — the POL-NS-07 anti-farming check. The open question for the reviewer is whether this driver's four no-show terminations in 30 days reflect genuine no-shows or fee-farming; on this particular trip the no-show is real (the rider was 851–858 m away throughout), but the trailing-30-day pattern is a judgement the automated pipeline is not permitted to make, and the reviewer must also decide the refund direction POL-NS-07 writes into the packet.\n\nON THE CLAIMS. All surviving claims were accepted: the arrival (POL-NS-01(a)), the 408-second dwell (POL-NS-01(c), POL-NS-02), the RIDER_NO_SHOW reason code after the dwell (POL-NS-01(d)), the non-false marker (POL-NS-05), the rider's absence (POL-NS-04), the clean fare ledger (POL-NS-08), and the withheld compensation (POL-NS-07/09). They do not conflict and they lead to the escalation above. Two claims about the MISSING traffic advisory (EV-ADVIS-02751-01, weight 0.0) were discarded by the referee for failing to name the MISSING_ARTIFACT issue code and are not relied on; nothing in this ruling turns on that artifact, whose absence only made POL-NS-06(i) unavailable, which is irrelevant because no accumulation was needed. The rider's lifetime prior_no_show_flags counter is context only under POL-GEN-01 and was used for no finding.\n\nCONFIDENCE. Every artifact carrying a deciding fact here — EV-TRIP-02751, EV-GPS-02751, EV-DPROF-02751 and EV-FARE-02751 — carries weight 1.0, so the POL-GEN-02(2) cap is 1.0. Confidence is set at 0.90, comfortably above the 0.70 escalation floor."
  },
